----------------------------------------------------------------
Japanese modifications (25Ja)
----------------------------------------------------------------

This derivative adds Japanese channel names / menus and related changes
to the Dondji source code. It is not an official Dondji product.

- FM station name display (ENABLE_FEAT_STERANIAN_DISP_RADIOSTATION_NAME)
  based on the idea in steranian/uv-k1-k5v3-firmware-custom;
  reimplemented with a dedicated station table (SPI 0x012000)
  https://github.com/steranian/uv-k1-k5v3-firmware-custom
  Copyright 2026 steranian, Apache License 2.0

- Japanese font data (web/font/25Ja_font_v4.bin, App/bdf/shinonome/)
  Shinonome 12-dot Gothic font, The Electronic Font Open Laboratory
  Public Domain (see App/bdf/shinonome/LICENSE)
  Source used: https://github.com/code4fukui/shinonome-font (053b21e)

- Fonts embedded in the firmware (inherited from Dondji / F4HWN; not added by 25Ja)
  App/ui/font_u8g2/ holds subsets of three bitmap fonts converted to u8g2 data,
  used for the frequency / small text on the dual-watch screen. Only a few
  glyphs of each are embedded (glyph counts from the file headers); the fonts
  are not distributed as font files. The terms below are as shown on the
  distribution sites (October 2026) and were not confirmed with the authors.
  * font_10_tr.h: "Small Bold Pixel-7", Copyright (c) 2013 Style-7
    (14 of 220 glyphs). Listed as "Freeware, Non-Commercial"; a commercial
    license is available from the designer. Commercial use of this firmware
    may therefore require a license for this font from the designer.
  * font_bn_tn.h: "Blocktopia", memesbruh03 (14 of 196 glyphs).
    Listed as "100% free".
  * font_5_tr.h: "SG04", Copyright (C) 2000 SHAKAGRAPHICS (64 of 104 glyphs).
    Only the copyright line was found; no usage terms were found.

- U8G2 graphics library (external/U8G2/)
  Copyright (c) 2016, olikraus@gmail.com, BSD 2-Clause License
  (the license text is in the header of each source file)
  https://github.com/olikraus/u8g2

- Changes made by 25Ja (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b)); modified files carry
  "JA:" comments in the source:
  * Japanese (kanji / kana) display: channel names (31 bytes, SPI back half
    0x020000), menu titles and values, SPI font (0x024000, 6647 characters)
  * FM station name table (SPI 0x012000)
  * Serial protocol: 25Ja identification in the hello reply, staged SPI write
    (0x0523), fixes for USB ring buffer / odd-length write handling
  * Settings screen: right-pane layout for two-line values containing kanji / kana
  * Keys: F+8 / F+9 backlight actions; scan list name refreshed immediately
    when the scan list is switched
  * Range scan: exclusion of the current frequency during scanning
    (MENU long press), ported from F4HWN 6.0.0 (Apache License 2.0)
  * Scan speed: "fast scan" (RSSI pre-check before stopping on a channel /
    frequency; menu "SetScn", Normal / Fast) and the RSSI graph shown while
    scanning, ported from F4HWN (armel/uv-k1-k5v3-firmware-custom,
    commit 3a50e212, Copyright armel et al., Apache License 2.0)
  * Scan list names in kanji / kana: SPI 0x008880, 12 bytes (UTF-8) x 24,
    shown in the menu (ScList / ChList) and in a pop-up when the scan list is
    switched while scanning
  * Serial protocol: 25Ja version number (major.minor.patch) returned in the
    hello reply (Padding[2]); EEPROM address map entry for 0x008880-0x0089A0
  * Menu: regrouped into five categories (Channel / Display-Audio / Keys /
    System / Scan), selected with new 24x24 launcher icons; many items
    renamed (Japanese titles); the scan list is called "scan group" in the
    Japanese menu. Items from "F Lock" on remain in the hidden menu
    (PTT + SIDE1 at power-on), as in Dondji / F4HWN.
  * Transmit power: the "USER" level was removed from the channel Power menu
    (Low1-5 / Mid / High remain); the global "SetPwr" item is hidden from the
    menu (the stored value is kept)
  * Boot hint: labels replaced with Japanese text in the Japanese menu;
    value 1 can show a 24-byte user text written by the CPS (SPI 0x0089A0)
  * Japanese labels for the side keys (PF1 / PF2); F Lock option "JA/CE HAM"
    (144-146 MHz / 430-440 MHz) in the Dondji F Lock list
  * Boot logo: replaced with an image made for 25Ja
  * MDC1200 / Yan ID signalling: disabled in the build (ENABLE_MDC_YAN_ID off)
  * Removed: TX 1750 Hz tone, Dondji web site / documentation / archive files
    and branding assets
